Looking at the shape, the only way to tile it completely with the five pieces (allowing rotations and flips) forces the 2×2 square piece D into the central 2×2 region marked by the dashed lines — exactly where the dot is located. The other pieces (the 3‑strip A, the L‑piece B, the T‑piece C, and the 5‑cell piece E) must fill the remaining arms and corners of the figure.

Therefore, the piece lying on the dot is D.

\boxed{D}
